  "rationale": "The requirement states one structural obligation. `Sources` must have a method `pub async fn search_structure(&self, query: &StructuralQuery) -> Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`.\n\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_structure]` has exactly that signature. It is `pub` and `async`, takes `&self` and `&StructuralQuery`, and returns `Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`. It sits in `impl Sources`, and `struct[Sources]` is defined in the same file. It delegates to `self.analysis.search_structure(query)`.\n- `self.analysis` is a `SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`, as shown by `struct[Sources]` and `impl[Sources]/fn[new]`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[search_structure]` returns `Result<StructuralMatches, P::Error>` by delegating to `self.provider.search_structure(query, &self.languages)`. `impl[LocalSources/SourceProvider]` declares `type Error = SourceError`, so the error type is `SourceError`. The `SourceProvider` trait's `search_structure` returns `StructuralMatches` in the `Ok` case.\n\nNo structural element is missing or conflicting. The requirement specifies only the signature, so I assessed no other behavior. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply and none are needed.",
